WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.321
A network trained on one sphere's flow.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.436
Its pink message tracks the exact velocity, using two numbers.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.980
Stokes flow has two parts: along the state, then along the offset.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.021
Theta: the angle between them.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.434
Sorted: exact b sub j, and exact a sub j.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.345
On the surface, fluid moves with the sphere, so the message equals q sub j.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.881
Now every position at once: learned left, exact right.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.425
Start with b sub j, along the state.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.258
Then a sub j, along the offset. It changes sign across the equator.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.919
The error is largest on the axis.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.887
Inside the training range, it averages two and a half percent.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.281
Past six radii, it saw no data. Exact b sub j keeps decaying.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.872
The learned one falls too fast: thirty-one percent error.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.030
The network learned a kernel: two functions of distance and angle.
